            "notes": "\ud83d\udccc Round 3 \ud83d\udccc\n\n\ud83c\udf80 Power : I also have two choices for you.\n\n- Option 1 [Fleet Foot](item_1d58371c-71a9-44c2-8d5a-0663467599e9) If your teammates can heal well or if your team needs to deal extra damage, you should choose this Power. So that you can go behind the enemy to cause chaos, the focus is not on killing them, but on causing chaos for the enemy to focus on you, making it easier for your teammates to play.\n\n- Option 2  [Two-Zu](item_80f16d3e-a4c0-4fa8-90b1-a0f033a1a77b) In fact, I don't recommend this option at all unless it's absolutely necessary, such as when your teammates can't heal or the enemy has  [Ana](hero_f1aee6cf-704f-455f-a100-ec882ebbe000)  or  [Ashe](hero_37b42a2d-a82d-4a22-9df2-4c812c873b54) As a skilled player, you should help your teammates first by using Suzu more often.\n\n\ud83d\udca1 Item :\n- I recommend you to buy items that increase WP%, it will make you deal more damage and heal, such as: [Hardlight Accelerator](item_0390c8af-2a68-4da2-b876-93da32c3f448) \n- If you choose  [Two-Zu](item_80f16d3e-a4c0-4fa8-90b1-a0f033a1a77b) It means that if you need more healing, you need to buy it.  [Talisman of Life](item_7ecfd3eb-d869-41fe-87eb-0bb2e82e5718) Before the item that greatly increases WP%\n\n\ud83d\udcd5 Playing style :\n- If you choose [Fleet Foot](item_1d58371c-71a9-44c2-8d5a-0663467599e9) You should try to sneak up behind your enemy to disrupt them as much as possible. You don't have to kill them, you just need to disrupt them.\n\n- If you choose [Two-Zu](item_80f16d3e-a4c0-4fa8-90b1-a0f033a1a77b) Focus on healing and saving your teammates. Don't waste Suzu too much. Use it when needed.",
